  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Tanzania Avocado supply chain mapping of travel costs and accomodation for local stakeholders</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The main purpose of the study is to provide a current overview of Tanzania&apos;s avocado sector by mapping out how it is structured through a holistic supply chain approach. This will shed light on the challenges the local supply chain actors are facing and the export potential, but also showcase data gaps for growth, efficiencies, needs by supply chain actors and display opportunities for innovative solution providers to enter the sector. The outcome to be achieved with the study is to stimulate supply chain actors, direct and indirect beneficiaries, to engage and adopt solutions and recommendations reported by the study. Ultimately, this can catalyse the sector&apos;s export potential and solidify Tanzanian avocados competitiveness on the global market.The project has a positive impact on:SDG 8: inclusive and sustainable economic growth: support productive activities, decent job creation, entrepreneurship, creativity and innovation.* The costs for this project were handled through project PSS22TZ01A.</narrative>
  </description>
